# Google Ads, managed with bidsmith

This repository describes a Google Ads account as code. The `.bid` files
are the source of truth; [bidsmith](https://github.com/chrmod/bidsmith)
makes the live account match them.

Every change goes through a pull request. The PR shows a `bidsmith plan`
diff — exactly what would change in Google Ads — and merging it applies
the change. Nothing touches the live account until a human merges.

## How it works

```
edit a .bid file  ──►  open a pull request  ──►  CI posts the plan
                                                       │
                                              review + merge to main
                                                       │
                                              CI runs `bidsmith apply`
                                                       │
                                                 Google Ads updated
```

- **Pull request** → `.github/workflows/bidsmith.yml` runs `bidsmith plan`
  and comments the diff on the PR.
- **Merge to main** → the same workflow runs `bidsmith apply` to reconcile
  the account.

## One-time setup

1. **Point at your account.** Edit [`bidsmith.toml`](./bidsmith.toml) and
   set `customer_id` and `login_customer_id` (no dashes).

2. **Add the credentials as GitHub Actions secrets.** In the repo:
   Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → *New repository secret*.
   Add all four:

   | Secret | Where it comes from |
   | --- | --- |
   | `GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN` | Your Google Ads manager account API centre |
   | `GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_ID` | Your OAuth client (or bidsmith's bundled one) |
   | `GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_SECRET` | Same OAuth client |
   | `GOOGLE_ADS_REFRESH_TOKEN` | `bidsmith auth login` prints/stores this |

   Run `bidsmith auth login` once locally to mint the refresh token, then
   `bidsmith auth profile --with-client` to read back the values to paste.

3. **Edit your campaigns.** Replace the placeholder content in
   [`campaigns.bid`](./campaigns.bid) and open a pull request.

## Working locally

```sh
bidsmith validate .     # check syntax, schema, references
bidsmith plan .         # preview the diff against the live account
```

`apply` runs in CI on merge — you rarely need to run it by hand. If you do,
`bidsmith apply .` prompts before changing anything.

Full docs: https://chrmod.github.io/bidsmith/
